WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
Insulin, a hormone, is
built from two short chains:

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.980
21 and 30 amino acids.

3
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:11.660
Titin, a protein in muscle,
has more than 30 thousand.

4
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:17.000
Yet every protein in your body is built
from the same twenty kinds of amino acid.

5
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.750
So how can so few building blocks
make so many different proteins?

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.520
In this mission, you'll meet
the one plan all twenty share,

7
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.750
and the one part that differs.

8
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.210
Then you'll join two amino acids, and
watch a water molecule leave as they bond.

9
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.530
Your mission: find out how just twenty
building blocks can make so many proteins.
